# Cloudflare Pages response headers for every route on 6502.dbhq.uk.
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# These apply AT THE EDGE ONLY. `astro preview` will not send them, so verify
# with `curl -I` against the deployed host, never against a local server.
#
# THE CSP ALLOWS EXACTLY ONE THIRD-PARTY ORIGIN, and it is Google Analytics.
# Everything else is 'self': no font host, no embed, no inline script.
# script-src has no 'unsafe-inline', which is why analytics.js and consent.js
# are same-origin files rather than Google's inline snippet.
#
# GA RUNS BY DEFAULT, ANALYTICS ONLY, WITH A NOTICE AND AN OPT-OUT, under the
# PECR statistical-purposes exception. The site launched on 1 Oct 2026 as
# opt-in, loading nothing until a visitor accepted, and moved to this the same
# day. Ad storage is denied and Signals and ad personalisation are off, which is
# what keeps it inside the exception; src/components/AnalyticsNotice.astro is
# the notice and "Cookie settings" in the footer reopens it. An opted-out
# visitor loads nothing from these origins at all. GA4 sets its cookie on the
# shared .dbhq.uk parent, so the opt-out is a cookie there too, and it holds
# across every dbhq.uk site.
#
# googletagmanager.com is in script-src and img-src; google-analytics.com is in
# img-src and connect-src and *.analytics.google.com in connect-src only, because GA beacons both
# as an image and as fetch/beacon depending on the browser. Dropping any one of
# them loses measurement silently rather than loudly. The list is the one the
# opt-in version already sent, unchanged: moving to opt-out changed when the
# origins are used, not which ones.
#
# script-src carries 'wasm-unsafe-eval' because each machine's page runs the
# machine as WebAssembly, and a browser compiles WebAssembly only when the CSP
# allows it. It permits WebAssembly compilation and nothing else: it does not
# allow eval() or new Function() for JavaScript, and the .wasm files are
# fetched from this site under connect-src 'self'. It applies site-wide rather
# than to the machines' pages alone because Pages joins the headers of every rule
# a path matches, and a second CSP on that path would narrow the first, not
# widen it.
#
# Two other relaxations, both narrow. style-src needs 'unsafe-inline' because
# Astro inlines every stylesheet (build.inlineStylesheets: 'always'), which keeps
# the first paint unblocked. img-src allows data: URIs for small inlined images,
# which cannot run script.
#
# Adding any further origin means asking what it sets and whether the notice
# covers it.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=15552000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'none'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://www.googletagmanager.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: https://www.googletagmanager.com https://www.google-analytics.com https://*.google-analytics.com; connect-src 'self' https://www.googletagmanager.com https://www.google-analytics.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com; manifest-src 'self'; frame-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
